"rationale": "The polling average sits around two points for Flanagan, and late September surveys show a dead-heat contest, while most expert raters still call it Likely D and markets price her near 90%. The evidence supports a Democratic favorite but a much narrower one than the ratings imply, so the forecast lands at a modest Democratic edge with elevated uncertainty.", "watch": "Whether late-breaking polls continue to tighten toward a true tossup, or outside spending and the fraud-scandal narrative fade, will determine if this moves to Likely D or Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Tina Smith (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Minnesota's open Senate seat has become unexpectedly competitive. Lieutenant Governor Peggy Flanagan leads former sportscaster Michele Tafoya by only about two points in recent polling, a sharp contrast with the state's three-point Democratic lean and the Likely D ratings from most expert observers. More than seven million dollars in outside spending has been directed against Flanagan, and coverage of her record has kept the race in the national spotlight.\n\nDespite the tight polls, prediction markets still give Flanagan roughly a 90% chance of winning, and the consensus of professional raters remains Likely D. The race appears closer than the fundamentals suggest, but the Democratic candidate retains the edge in a state Republicans have not carried in a Senate race in years.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8725, "margin": 5.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7776, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8131, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8217, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7867, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.784, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7719, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7956, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7935, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_d